  {
    "label": "figure_title",
    "text": "FIG. 3. From arena to circular channels. a. Experimental snapshots of a binary mixture confined in an annular channel for different values of Rin/Rout, showing the progressive loss of radial demixing as the inner radius increases. b. Corresponding simulation snapshots obtained under the same conditions, reproducing the transition from a demixed to a mixed state. c. Steady-state demixing parameter from numerical simulations, (γ)t, as a function of Rin/Rout for experiments and simulations. Demixing decreases monotonically with increasing Rin/Rout, demonstrating that the relative curvature of the inner and outer boundaries controls the efficiency of radial segregation.",
